'''Line 6: Maru no Uchi no Sanzu no Kawa''' (Japanese: 丸ノ内ノ三途ノ川, lit. '''The River Sanzu Within a Circle''') is the sixth line of [[Refraction Railway]] introduced in [[Season 7: Kumo no ito • oti on akA]]. It is unlocked by completing [[Canto IX]].

Line 6 is composed of 8 total Stations, divided into 5 Sections. Each Station offer difficult Encounters based on enemies encountered in [[Canto IX]] or [[Intervallo V - 1]], [[Peccatulum|Peccatula Invidiae]] of various Identities, and 3 new Abnormalities that had E.G.O available from [[Season 6]] and Season 7's battle passes. <br> The Stations in each Section are treated as multiple waves of a single Encounter.

Line 6 uses the Chain Battle mechanic, with all Sinners being required to be Deployed before the start of the battle, with the last 5 Sinners reserved as Backup. Backup Units receive bonus Starting SP, with Minus Coin Identities gaining negative Starting SP buffs instead. Identities also give E.G.O resources upon death according to their Sin Affinities: Identity death gives 1 Skill 1-Affinity resource, 2 Skill 2-Affinity resources, and 3 Skill 3-Affinity resources.

The team loadout can be changed after the completion of each Section. With the exception of Section 5, entering a new section will revive all defeated allies, restore their HP to full, and reset their SP to 0. Section 5 will instead use the team's HP percentage and SP at the point of clearing Section 1. <br>
Sections 3 and 4 will restrict the use of any Identities deployed in the loadout in the immediately preceding Section. That is, the Identities deployed in Section 2 cannot be deployed for Section 3, and the Identities deployed for Section 3 cannot be deployed for Section 4. Sections 2 and 5 have no restrictions on deployable Identities.

